---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
const topics = [
  ["Compatibility boundaries", "compatibility"],
  ["FAQ", "faq"],
] as const;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Compatibility & support"
  description="Choose workloads that fit Mimic and understand its current boundaries."
  topics={topics}
>
  <h2 id="compatibility">Compatibility boundaries</h2>
  <p>
    Mimic models observable browser state without a native rendering pipeline.
    Use a full browser when accurate rendered pixels are the desired output.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      No native renderer.{" "}
      <code>Page.captureScreenshot</code> returns an
      approximate PNG of the current Page. Visual accuracy is not
      guaranteed; the image may differ from Chrome and from Mimic's modeled
      geometry. See the{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/mimic-browser/runtime/blob/main/docs/approximate-screenshots.md"
        >screenshot limitations</a
      >. Rendered PDFs and video output are unsupported.
    </li>
    <li>
      Modeled geometry and input are not complete CSS layout, clipping, rich
      editing, touch, drag, or arbitrary transforms.
    </li>
    <li>
      CDP and Web API coverage is partial. Generated names and wire schema do
      not imply implemented semantics.
    </li>
    <li>
      Compatibility checks describe specific workflows—not every website, client
      option, or anti-bot decision.
    </li>
    <li>
      The CDP endpoint has no authentication; bind it only where trusted clients
      can reach it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Is Mimic headless Chrome?</summary>
      <p>
        No. It uses V8 for JavaScript but does not embed or launch Chromium.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Does every website work?</summary>
      <p>
        No. Compatibility is actively expanding and depends on the APIs, loading
        behavior, and interactions a workflow uses.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Can I run untrusted code?</summary>
      <p>
        No. Mimic is not a security sandbox, and separate Pages are not
        hostile-tenant security boundaries.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Is Mimic open source?</summary>
      <p>
        Mimic's source is public under the Prosperity Public License 3.0.0.
        Noncommercial use is free; commercial use has a 30-day trial. Read the{" "}
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}license/`}>license</a> for the full
        terms.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
